Adversarial probe (expected, not observed): the test `should return true when age is exactly 18 (spec boundary...)` is expected to **fail** — not from a setup/import/fixture problem, but because `isAdult(18)` evaluates `18 > 18` → `false`, while the stated correctness contract (`18 or over is an adult`) requires `true`. All other tests are expected to pass against the current source as written, since they characterize existing (if arguably risky) behavior rather than asserting undeclared requirements.

## Handoffs
→ ndv-diagnose (root cause) · `src/age.js:2`: off-by-one boundary bug — `age > 18` excludes exactly-18 from adulthood, contradicting the stated contract "a person aged 18 or over is an adult". Fix is `age >= 18`; do not edit here, this is a test file.
